---
import Root from '#/layout/root.astro'
import Callout from '#/components/callout.astro'
---

<Root title="About Me">
  <div class="flow prose">
    <h1>About Me</h1>
    <p>
      I started working with the web at the tender age of 13 making websites to
      host my serious literature<sup>*</sup>. Since then I've studied electronic
      hardware design at Southampton University, worked as a secondary school
      Computer Science teacher for seven years, and returned to web development.
    </p><p>
      Suffice to say, I've been thinking about computers and the web for a <em>
        long time
      </em>, and my time as a teacher has also given me the skillset to explain
      the tools, technology, and techniques I use to clients and project
      stakeholders.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm">* Nintendo fanfiction</p>
    <Callout>
      Looking for something more formal and/or detailed? <a
        href="/DRB_CV.pdf"
        target="_blank"
      >
        Download my CV.
      </a>
    </Callout>
  </div>
  <section class="with-sidebar">
    <div class="sidebar flow">
      <h2>Work History</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="flow">
      <h3>???</h3>
      <span class="text-sm text-lowlight">
        Due to redundancy I'm looking for new opportunities in Q4 2026 - <a
          href="mailto:dan@mxbranch.com?subject=I'm Looking For A Web Developer"
        >
          Get in touch with me via email!
        </a>
      </span>
      <h3>Under One Cloud</h3>
      <span class="text-sm text-lowlight">
        Lead Software Developer, 2022 to 2026
      </span>
      <p>
        Initially hired to maintain legacy .NET Framework projects, and helped
        transition the company into providing web development services for our
        clients. Led teams and worked solo to ship full stack web applications,
        marketing websites, and software integrations.
      </p>
      <p>
        Delivered a full rebuild of a Learning Management System for a
        professional development company, who were able to expand their
        eLearning operation to ~1800 users and counting. The client was so
        pleased with the result that they contracted UOC for further development
        of features.
      </p>
      <h3>Cantell School</h3>
      <span class="text-sm text-lowlight">
        Computer Science Teacher, 2016 to 2022
      </span>
      <p>
        Led the GCSE Computer Science curriculum with students across all
        classes performing above the national average every year. Helped
        redevelop the KS3 curriculum on the topics of programming and computer
        hardware, including creating a syllabus and lesson plans to teach
        programming fundamentals for use by other staff members. Ran a D&D club
        and pretended to be several elves.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="with-sidebar">
    <div class="sidebar flow">
      <h2>Skills and Interests</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-lowlight">
        This is a non-exhaustive list, and I'm eager to pick up new languages,
        frameworks, and libraries!
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="flow">
      <h3>Web Fundamentals</h3>
      <ul role="list">
        <li>Use of semantic HTML</li>
        <li>Modern CSS features and methodologies</li>
        <li>Tailwind</li>
        <li>Vanilla JavaScript + TypeScript</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Frameworks</h3>
      <ul role="list">
        <li>React + Next.js (App Router + Server Components)</li>
        <li>Astro</li>
        <li>CMSs (Payload)</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Back End</h3>
      <ul role="list">
        <li>Node</li>
        <li>REST APIs</li>
        <li>ORMs (Drizzle, Prisma)</li>
        <li>SQL + MySQL/MariaDB/Postgres</li>
        <li>Docker</li>
        <li>Linux Servers</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Design</h3>
      <ul role="list">
        <li>Design Systems and Component Libraries</li>
        <li>Accessibility in Web Design</li>
        <li></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Root>
